A request over the form bounds fails, and is never cut

Upstream's post iterator keeps every non-file field of a form body in
the request's map before any endpoint runs: max_post_param_size cuts a
longer field to its length, and nothing bounds the number of fields or
their total. A cut value can still read as a valid one, every new field
is a scan of the map, and the memory is held for as long as the body
takes. With this change a field over max_post_param_size (a key sent
more than once counts as its values joined, as the map keeps them),
fields that together pass max_post_body_size, or more than ULFIUS_MAX_POST_FIELDS
(256) fields make the iterator refuse the body, and a body the post
processor refuses ends the request (the dispatcher answers MHD_NO): no
endpoint runs on the fields that were kept.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Scott Wiederhold <s.e.wiederhold@gmail.com>

